# Notebook ↔ Web app parity

When changing **Bloom evaluation**, **improve & re-evaluate**, or **course-generation pipeline** logic:

1. Update **both** the web app and `course-generation-algorithm.ipynb` unless the user explicitly scopes one side only.
2. Keep these in sync (same constants, same behavior):

| Web app | Notebook |
|---------|----------|
| `src/lib/bloom/problem-slides.ts` | Step 3.5 constants + `select_problem_slides` |
| `src/server/services/bloom-improve.ts` | Step 3.5 `improve_and_reevaluate_from_bloom` |
| `src/server/ai/prompts/bloom-improvement.ts` | Step 3.5 `build_bloom_improvement_instructions` |
| `src/server/ai/prompts/single-slide.ts` | Step 3.5 `regenerate_single_slide` |
| `src/server/ai/prompts/evaluation.ts` | Step 3 `evaluate_deck` prompts |
| `src/lib/cqi/v1.ts` | Step 5 CQI weights + LRS/CQI formulas + DQP rules |
| `src/server/ai/prompts/cqi-engagement.ts` | Step 5 `evaluate_engagement_metrics` |

3. Shared limits (change in both places):
   - `BLOOM_TARGET_SCORE = 95`
   - `BLOOM_MAX_IMPROVE_ROUNDS = 3`
   - `BLOOM_MAX_PROBLEM_SLIDES = 8`

4. After edits, note in the commit/PR if notebook and app were updated together.
